    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Parts a and b use a direct complement, 1 − 0.8^n. Part c is the hardest demand: the student must turn 'greater than 0.95' into 0.8^n < 0.05, then solve it by trial or logarithms and interpret the result as a whole number of casts. There is no tree, table or hint, but the model and method are routine for a prepared student. It is harder than the tree-based complement work in p44-q5, but well below p38-q23, which also needs a two-way table.",
